## Third-party components pulled at build time

The component pulls Espressif sources through the ESP-IDF component manager at
build time (`espressif/esp_video`, `esp_cam_sensor`, `esp_ipa`, `esp_sccb_intf`,
`esp_h264`, optionally `usb_host_uvc`). None of them are vendored here; they
carry their own licenses and are fetched from https://components.espressif.com/.
As shipped in the versions this component pins (checked 2026-07): `esp_video`
and `esp_ipa` are under the ESPRESSIF MIT License; `esp_cam_sensor`,
`esp_sccb_intf`, `esp_h264` and `usb_host_uvc` are under Apache-2.0.

`components/esp_video_camera/cfg/sc202cs.json` is an IPA (image tuning)
configuration file taken from the original pull request.

## In Tessera's screen_camera plugin

This folder is the component as published at github.com/n-IA-hane/esphome-esp-video-camera, release v2026.9.2
(commit 6d247d7), copied without changes. The plugin's own code is in `components/screen_camera/`.

## The OV02C10 in Tessera's copy

For the Guition ESP32-P4 screens this copy adds an OV02C10 sensor driver and its image tuning, written and first
tried on a Guition JC8012P4A1 V3 by Jeroen Peters (@Heronimonimo) in a stand-alone plugin that this replaces:

  * `ov02c10_sensor.c`, `ov02c10.h`, `ov02c10_compat.h`, `ov02c10_regs.h`, `ov02c10_settings.h` and
    `ov02c10_types.h`: copied from https://github.com/sullb/esphome-p4-csi-camera (MIT License, below) on
    2026-10-18. That project identifies the register tables as based on the Linux OV02C10 driver; the driver
    follows the structure of Espressif's esp_cam_sensor drivers (Apache-2.0, see their SPDX headers). Changed on
    2026-10-19, as its header says: exposure, gain and orientation on the sensor's own registers (as
    drivers/media/i2c/ov02c10.c in Linux sets them), OV5640 registers removed, the chip id checked.
  * `build_stubs/ov02c10_ipa/ov02c10_p4_eco5.json` and `ov02c10_p4_eco4.json`: image tuning derived from
    Espressif's `sc2336_default_p4_eco4.json` (esp_cam_sensor, Apache-2.0), with the black level and gamma of its
    rev3 tunings in the eco5 file; `CMakeLists.txt` and `project_include.cmake` beside them are new.
  * `esp_video_camera.cpp` calls `ov02c10_sensor_link_anchor()` and `__init__.py` adds the tuning; both places
    are marked "Tessera" or "OV02C10".

